<title>UK: CRICKET-BENSON AND HEDGES CUP RESULTS.</title>
<headline>CRICKET-BENSON AND HEDGES CUP RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results of Benson and Hedges Cup</p>
<p>(50 overs) cricket matches on Wednesday:</p>
<p>At Fenners: British Universities beat Sussex by 19 runs.</p>
<p>British Universities 217-6 innings closed. Sussex 198 in 48.3</p>
<p>overs (V.Drakes 58; M.Chilton 5-26).</p>
<p>At Chester-le-Street: Durham beat Northamptonshire by 64</p>
<p>runs. Durham 225-6 innings closed (D.Boon 103). Northamptonshire</p>
<p>161 in 42.5 overs (R.Bailey 62; S.Brown 6-30).</p>
<p>At Bristol: Surrey beat Gloucestershire by three wickets.</p>
<p>Gloucestershire 280-7 innings closed (R.Cunliffe 113, S.Young</p>
<p>67). Surrey 282-7 in 49.2 overs (B.Hollioake 69, A.Brown 66).</p>
<p>At Canterbury: Kent beat Hampshire by two wickets. Hampshire</p>
<p>207 in 49.5 overs (M.Fleming 5-27). Kent 211-8 in 45.4 overs</p>
<p>(M.Walker 83, N.Llong 55).</p>
<p>At Old Trafford: Derbyshire beat Lancashire by six wickets.</p>
<p>Lancashire 223 in 44 overs (J.Gallian 52). Derbyshire 225-4 in</p>
<p>48.3 overs (K.Barnett 112 not out).</p>
<p>At Leicester: Leicestershire beat Nottinghamshire by 77</p>
<p>runs. Leicestershire 295-7 innings closed (D.Maddy 101, V.Wells</p>
<p>70). Nottinghamshire 218 in 47.4 overs.</p>
<p>At Lord's: Essex beat Middlesex by one wicket. Middlesex</p>
<p>226-8 innings closed (M.Ramprakash 77, J.Pooley 50 not out).</p>
<p>Essex 227-9 innings closed (S.Law 53).</p>
<p>At Taunton: Somerset beat Glamorgan by 141 runs. Somerset</p>
<p>258-9 innings closed (M.Lathwell 77, R.Harden 68). Glamorgan 117</p>
<p>in 30.4 overs.</p>
<p>At Edgbaston: Warwickshire beat Minor Counties by 155 runs.</p>
<p>Warwickshire 261-7 innings closed (D.Brown 62, A.Moles 60).</p>
<p>Minor Counties 106 in 32.4 overs (G.Small 5-23).</p>
<p>At Headingley: Worcestershire beat Yorkshire by 12 runs.</p>
<p>Worcestershire 199-9 innings closed. Yorkshire 187-7 innings</p>
<p>closed (P.Newport 4-37).</p>
</text>
